      },
      "lineNbr": 711,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-24T16:49:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This version of the chip only supports one UCPD port. The G0 does support 2 ports and my intention was to make the driver. I will add another TODO for now. My plan was to include some macros that maps PD port number to UCPC port number. In addition my thought was to replace \u0027port\u0027 in the function prototypes with \u0027usbc_port\u0027 then all ucpd register accesses can remain \u0027port\u0027 as they are now.\n\nThis is not an issue for honeybuns as there is only 1 ucpd port and that\u0027s used for the host port which is port 0 as well. But, for the driver to be complete, it needs the change I mentioned.",
      "parentUuid": "05366649_d3225d59",
      "revId": "330236a1e8b03ed8fe67f6098b9036093c4fb4fa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
